IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Northwest Territories income assistance -- the applicant's and recipient's duties and deadlines, and what the Officer
-- must give them, kept apart from nt-sa.l4 so that only this module loads the date library.
--   IA Regulations s 19(1) and SPD Regulations s 19(1): reporting a change; IA s 10(3) and SPD s 11(5): proof of applying
--   for a social insurance number; SPD s 11(2), (3): the information and documents; IA s 14 and SPD s 14: the refusal and
--   its written reasons; Act s 13: no false or misleading statement.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Duties under the Social Assistance Act and its regulations`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant`
    `the Officer`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `inform the Officer of the change in circumstances`
    `provide proof of having applied for a social insurance number`
    `provide the information and documents required by SPD s 11(2)`
    `inform the applicant of the refusal and give written reasons`
    `make a false or misleading statement to obtain assistance`

§§ `Dates`

-- The same day a number of months later, or the last day of that month if it is shorter.
GIVEN `day` IS A DATE, `months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the same day months later` `day` `months` MEANS
    IF DATE_DAY `day` AT MOST `days in` m2 y2
    THEN Date (DATE_DAY `day`) m2 y2
    ELSE Date (`days in` m2 y2) m2 y2
    WHERE
        k  MEANS (DATE_MONTH `day` MINUS 1) PLUS `months`
        m2 MEANS (k MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        y2 MEANS DATE_YEAR `day` PLUS FLOOR (k DIVIDED BY 12)

GIVEN `month` IS A NUMBER, `year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`days in` `month` `year` MEANS
    (Date 1 m2 y2) MINUS (Date 1 `month` `year`)
    WHERE
        m2 MEANS (`month` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        y2 MEANS `year` PLUS FLOOR (`month` DIVIDED BY 12)

-- The first day of the month after the month of a given day.
GIVEN `day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the first of the month after` `day` MEANS
    Date 1 m2 y2
    WHERE
        m2 MEANS (DATE_MONTH `day` MODULO 12) PLUS 1
        y2 MEANS DATE_YEAR `day` PLUS FLOOR (DATE_MONTH `day` DIVIDED BY 12)

§§ `Reporting a change`

-- IA s 19(1): "A recipient shall inform an Officer, on or before the first of the month following the month in which
-- assistance is provided, of any change in circumstances that may affect the amount of assistance ..., including but not
-- limited to a change in family members, income, assets or residence." Read for a change in a month for which assistance
-- is provided: by the first of the next month. If not: the Officer "shall terminate assistance" (s 20(1)(c)) or may give
-- one formal warning instead (s 20(2) to (4)), and the recipient is ineligible for the month, or two months on a repeat
-- (s 5).
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to report a change under IA s 19(1)` `the day of the change` MEANS `the first of the month after` `the day of the change`

-- SPD s 19(1): "A recipient shall, within 60 days of the change, inform an Officer of any change in the recipient's
-- circumstances that may affect their eligibility or status as a person in need or the amount of assistance". If not:
-- termination (s 20(1)(c)) or a warning (s 20(2)), and ineligibility under s 6.
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to report a change under SPD s 19(1)` `the day of the change` MEANS `the day of the change` PLUS 60

-- Time is counted in days from the day of the change.
DECLARE `Stream` IS ONE OF
    `the Income Assistance Regulations`
    `the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations`

GIVEN `stream` IS A `Stream`, `the day of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to report a change` `stream` `the day of the change` MEANS
    CONSIDER `stream`
    WHEN `the Income Assistance Regulations` THEN `the last day to report a change under IA s 19(1)` `the day of the change`
    WHEN `the Seniors and Persons with Disabilities Regulations` THEN `the last day to report a change under SPD s 19(1)` `the day of the change`

GIVEN `stream` IS A `Stream`, `the day of the change` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to report a change` `stream` `the day of the change` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `inform the Officer of the change in circumstances`
    WITHIN (`the last day to report a change` `stream` `the day of the change`) MINUS `the day of the change`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "change not reported in time (IA or SPD s 19(1)); the Officer must terminate assistance or may give one formal warning (s 20(1)(c), (2)), and the recipient is ineligible for the month (IA s 5, SPD s 6)"

§§ `Proof of a social insurance number`

-- IA s 10(3) and SPD s 11(5): if proof of a social insurance number is not available at the date of the application, the
-- applicant "shall, within two months after that date, provide proof that (a) the applicant has applied for a social
-- insurance number; or (b) in the case of a mature dependant, the mature dependant has applied".
GIVEN `the date of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to prove a social insurance number application` `the date of the application` MEANS
    `the same day months later` `the date of the application` 2

GIVEN `the date of the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to prove a social insurance number application` `the date of the application` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `provide proof of having applied for a social insurance number`
    WITHIN (`the last day to prove a social insurance number application` `the date of the application`) MINUS `the date of the application`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "no proof of a social insurance number application within two months after the application (IA s 10(3), SPD s 11(5))"

§§ `SPD s 11 -- the information and documents`

-- SPD s 11(3): the information and documents in s 11(2) (including, for a person with a disability, a medical
-- professional's certificate, and the net annual income) "must be provided within 60 days of the date of application for
-- assistance or within such other time within the eligibility period as may be permitted by the Officer". (4)(b): the
-- Officer "shall ... refuse an application" if they are not received in time.
GIVEN `the date of the application` IS A DATE, `days the Officer allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day to provide the SPD s 11(2) documents` `the date of the application` `days the Officer allows` MEANS
    `the date of the application` PLUS (IF `days the Officer allows` GREATER THAN 60 THEN `days the Officer allows` ELSE 60)

GIVEN `the date of the application` IS A DATE, `days the Officer allows` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty to provide the SPD documents` `the date of the application` `days the Officer allows` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    MUST  `provide the information and documents required by SPD s 11(2)`
    WITHIN (`the last day to provide the SPD s 11(2) documents` `the date of the application` `days the Officer allows`) MINUS `the date of the application`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "information and documents not provided within 60 days or the time the Officer allowed; the Officer must refuse the application (SPD s 11(4)(b))"

§§ `IA s 14, SPD s 14 -- the refusal and its reasons`

-- IA s 14 and SPD s 14: an Officer "shall refuse assistance to any applicant whom the Officer determines is not a person in
-- need or is not eligible ..., and shall, within three business days of a decision to refuse, (a) inform the applicant of
-- the decision; and (b) provide written reasons for the refusal." The same duty follows a refusal for want of information
-- (IA s 12(3), SPD s 13(3)). Business days depend on the holiday calendar, so the number of calendar days to the third
-- business day is an input.
GIVEN `calendar days to the third business day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`what I must be given on a refusal` `calendar days to the third business day` MEANS
    PARTY `the Officer`
    MUST  `inform the applicant of the refusal and give written reasons`
    WITHIN `calendar days to the third business day`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the Officer` BECAUSE "the applicant was not told of the refusal with written reasons within three business days (IA s 14, SPD s 14)"

§§ `Act s 13 -- no false statement`

-- Act s 13: "No person shall make a false or misleading statement for the purpose of obtaining assistance or welfare
-- services for himself or herself or any other person." s 15: an offence punishable on summary conviction. IA s 4 and
-- SPD s 5: ineligible for the month the Director so determines (two months on a repeat). The period watched is an input.
GIVEN `days watched` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`my duty not to make a false statement` `days watched` MEANS
    PARTY `the applicant`
    SHANT `make a false or misleading statement to obtain assistance`
    WITHIN `days watched`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `the applicant` BECAUSE "false or misleading statement to obtain assistance: an offence (Act ss 13, 15) and ineligibility for the month (IA s 4, SPD s 5)"
